IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`

-- coa-definitions.l4: the Act's own definitions and interpretation provisions in the keel's ranges of
-- ukpga-2006-46.txt: lines 1-55 (Part 1, ss 1-6) and lines 16446-16624 (Part 38, ss 1158-1174).
-- Each defined term is a function over plain facts; the nouns are in coa-core.l4.
--
-- SOURCE. A plain-text rendering of the Act from legislation.gov.uk made by a converter script; it is not the
-- official text and nothing here is "verified against the official text". Quote lines are checked by srcrefs.py.
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER (the rule of 2026-10-29, assumed, not ruled by a lawyer). Every definition function
-- answers MAYBE BOOLEAN, with one exception (a total table, noted where it occurs).
--   JUST TRUE   the text says the case is within the term.
--   JUST FALSE  the text says no in its own words ("means", "if", "only if", "while", "where", a flat negative
--               such as "does not include"). Each such branch carries a comment
--               -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "<the quoted words>"
--   NOTHING     the text does not decide: it lists without closing the list, says "includes", leaves a term
--               undefined, is silent, points outside the sources, or limits a grant by its own wording.
--               Each such branch carries a comment -- NOTHING-kind (<why>), <why> being one of: silent,
--               list not closed, includes, undefined term, points outside the text, limited by its own wording.
--   A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
--
-- BORROWED TERMS. Where a definition is handed to another Act, an EU instrument or a body outside the sources, the
-- borrowed answer is an INPUT of type MAYBE BOOLEAN: JUST TRUE or JUST FALSE as the borrowed definition says,
-- NOTHING where it is not known; NOTHING passes through as NOTHING (points outside the text).
--
-- Every name that is not in coa-core.l4 begins with the section label it implements, as the keel's naming rule says.

-- =========================================================================================================
-- PART 1: GENERAL INTRODUCTORY PROVISIONS (lines 6-55)
-- =========================================================================================================

-- ---- s 1: Companies --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:9 | (1) In the Companies Acts, unless the context otherwise requires—
-- src:10 | “company” means a company formed and registered under this Act, that is—
-- src:11 | (a) a company so formed and registered after the commencement of this Part, or
-- src:12 | (b) a company that immediately before the commencement of this Part—
-- src:13 | (i) was formed and registered under the Companies Act 1985 (c. 6) or the Companies (Northern Ireland) Order 1986 (S.I. 1986/1032 (N.I. 6)), or
-- src:14 | (ii) was an existing company for the purposes of that Act or that Order,
-- src:15 | (which is to be treated on commencement as if formed and registered under this Act).
@ref s 1(1) Companies (src:9-15)
GIVEN `formed and registered under this Act after the commencement of Part 1` IS A BOOLEAN
      `immediately before that commencement formed and registered under the Companies Act 1985 or the Companies (Northern Ireland) Order 1986` IS A BOOLEAN
      `immediately before that commencement an existing company for the purposes of that Act or that Order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the context otherwise requires` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1(1) the body is a company` MEANS
    IF `the context otherwise requires`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "unless the context otherwise requires"
    ELSE IF       `formed and registered under this Act after the commencement of Part 1`
             OR   `immediately before that commencement formed and registered under the Companies Act 1985 or the Companies (Northern Ireland) Order 1986`
             OR   `immediately before that commencement an existing company for the purposes of that Act or that Order`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“company” means a company formed and registered under this Act"

-- src:16 | (2) Certain provisions of the Companies Acts apply to—
-- src:17 | (a) companies registered, but not formed, under this Act (see Chapter 1 of Part 33), and
-- src:18 | (b) bodies incorporated in the United Kingdom but not registered under this Act (see Chapter 2 of that Part).
@ref s 1(2) Certain provisions apply to other bodies (src:16-18)
GIVEN `registered, but not formed, under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1(2)(a) Chapter 1 of Part 33 applies to the company` MEANS
    IF `registered, but not formed, under this Act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Certain provisions of the Companies Acts apply to"

GIVEN `incorporated in the United Kingdom but not registered under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1(2)(b) Chapter 2 of Part 33 applies to the body` MEANS
    IF `incorporated in the United Kingdom but not registered under this Act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Certain provisions of the Companies Acts apply to"

-- src:19 | (3) For provisions applying to companies incorporated outside the United Kingdom, see Part 34 (overseas companies).
@ref s 1(3) Companies incorporated outside the United Kingdom (src:19)
GIVEN `incorporated outside the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1(3) Part 34 is where the Companies Acts deal with the company` MEANS
    IF `incorporated outside the United Kingdom`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "For provisions applying to companies incorporated outside the United Kingdom, see Part 34"

-- ---- s 2: The Companies Acts -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

DECLARE `s 2 enactment` IS ONE OF
    `s 2 the Companies Act 2006`
    `s 2 the Companies (Audit, Investigations and Community Enterprise) Act 2004`
    `s 2 the Companies Act 1985`
    `s 2 the Companies Consolidation (Consequential Provisions) Act 1985`
    `s 2 another enactment`

DECLARE `s 2 place in the enactment` IS ONE OF
    `s 2 in a Part` HAS `s 2 Part number` IS A NUMBER
    `s 2 in a Schedule`

DECLARE `s 2 provision` HAS
    `s 2 enactment of the provision` IS A `s 2 enactment`
    `s 2 place of the provision` IS A `s 2 place in the enactment`
    `remaining in force` IS A BOOLEAN
    `applying for the purposes of Parts 1 to 39` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:25 | (2) The company law provisions of this Act are—
-- src:26 | (a) the provisions of Parts 1 to 39 of this Act, and
-- src:27 | (b) the provisions of Parts 45 to 47 of this Act so far as they apply for the purposes of those Parts.
@ref s 2(2) The company law provisions of this Act (src:25-27)
GIVEN p IS A `s 2 provision`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(2) the provision is a company law provision of this Act` MEANS
    CONSIDER p's `s 2 enactment of the provision`
    WHEN `s 2 the Companies Act 2006` THEN
        CONSIDER p's `s 2 place of the provision`
        WHEN `s 2 in a Part` n THEN
            BRANCH
                IF n AT LEAST 1 AND n AT MOST 39 THEN JUST TRUE
                IF n AT LEAST 45 AND n AT MOST 47 THEN
                    IF p's `applying for the purposes of Parts 1 to 39`
                    THEN JUST TRUE
                    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) the provisions of Parts 45 to 47 of this Act so far as they apply for the purposes of those Parts"
                OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The company law provisions of this Act are— (a) the provisions of Parts 1 to 39 of this Act, and (b) the provisions of Parts 45 to 47"
        WHEN `s 2 in a Schedule` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the list names Parts, not Schedules
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the company law provisions of this Act"

-- src:21 | (1) In this Act “the Companies Acts” means—
-- src:22 | (a) the company law provisions of this Act,
-- src:23 | (b) Part 2 of the Companies (Audit, Investigations and Community Enterprise) Act 2004 (c. 27) (community interest companies), and
-- src:24 | (c) the provisions of the Companies Act 1985 (c. 6) and the Companies Consolidation (Consequential Provisions) Act 1985 (c. 9) that remain in force.
@ref s 2(1) The Companies Acts (src:21-24)
GIVEN p IS A `s 2 provision`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) the provision is one of the Companies Acts` MEANS
    CONSIDER p's `s 2 enactment of the provision`
    WHEN `s 2 the Companies Act 2006` THEN `s 2(2) the provision is a company law provision of this Act` p
    WHEN `s 2 the Companies (Audit, Investigations and Community Enterprise) Act 2004` THEN
        CONSIDER p's `s 2 place of the provision`
        WHEN `s 2 in a Part` n THEN
            IF n EQUALS 2
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In this Act “the Companies Acts” means— ... (b) Part 2 of the Companies (Audit, Investigations and Community Enterprise) Act 2004"
        WHEN `s 2 in a Schedule` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): paragraph (b) names Part 2, not a Schedule to it
    WHEN `s 2 the Companies Act 1985` THEN
        IF p's `remaining in force`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the provisions of the Companies Act 1985 (c. 6) and the Companies Consolidation (Consequential Provisions) Act 1985 (c. 9) that remain in force"
    WHEN `s 2 the Companies Consolidation (Consequential Provisions) Act 1985` THEN
        IF p's `remaining in force`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the provisions of the Companies Act 1985 (c. 6) and the Companies Consolidation (Consequential Provisions) Act 1985 (c. 9) that remain in force"
    WHEN `s 2 another enactment` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In this Act “the Companies Acts” means—"

-- ---- s 3: Limited and unlimited companies ----------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:30 | (1) A company is a “limited company” if the liability of its members is limited by its constitution.
-- src:31 | It may be limited by shares or limited by guarantee.
@ref s 3(1) Limited company (src:30-31)
GIVEN liability IS A `Liability of members`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 3(1) the company is a limited company` MEANS
    CONSIDER liability
    WHEN `liability not limited` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A company is a “limited company” if the liability of its members is limited by its constitution"
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:32 | (2) If their liability is limited to the amount, if any, unpaid on the shares held by them, the company is “limited by shares”.
@ref s 3(2) Limited by shares (src:32)
GIVEN liability IS A `Liability of members`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 3(2) the company is limited by shares` MEANS
    CONSIDER liability
    WHEN `liability limited to the amount, if any, unpaid on the shares held` THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If their liability is limited to the amount, if any, unpaid on the shares held by them, the company is “limited by shares”"

-- src:33 | (3) If their liability is limited to such amount as the members undertake to contribute to the assets of the company in the event of its being wound up, the company is “limited by guarantee”.
@ref s 3(3) Limited by guarantee (src:33)
GIVEN liability IS A `Liability of members`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 3(3) the company is limited by guarantee` MEANS
    CONSIDER liability
    WHEN `liability limited to the amount the members undertake to contribute on a winding up` THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If their liability is limited to such amount as the members undertake to contribute to the assets of the company in the event of its being wound up, the company is “limited by guarantee”"

-- src:34 | (4) If there is no limit on the liability of its members, the company is an “unlimited company”.
@ref s 3(4) Unlimited company (src:34)
GIVEN liability IS A `Liability of members`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 3(4) the company is an unlimited company` MEANS
    CONSIDER liability
    WHEN `liability not limited` THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If there is no limit on the liability of its members, the company is an “unlimited company”"

-- ---- s 4: Private and public companies -------------------------------------------------------------------

-- The three s 4 rules take a company: whether the body is a "company" at all is s 1(1).

-- src:40 | (3) For the purposes of subsection (2)(b) the relevant date is—
-- src:41 | (a) in relation to registration or re-registration in Great Britain, 22nd December 1980;
-- src:42 | (b) in relation to registration or re-registration in Northern Ireland, 1st July 1983.
@ref s 4(3) The relevant date (src:40-42)
GIVEN place IS A `Place of registration`
GIVETH A DATE
`s 4(3) the relevant date` MEANS
    CONSIDER place
    WHEN `Northern Ireland` THEN Date 1 7 1983
    OTHERWISE Date 22 12 1980 -- "Great Britain" is England and Wales together with Scotland

-- src:37 | (2) A “public company” is a company limited by shares or limited by guarantee and having a share capital—
-- src:38 | (a) whose certificate of incorporation states that it is a public company, and
-- src:39 | (b) in relation to which the requirements of this Act, or the former Companies Acts, as to registration or re-registration as a public company have been complied with on or after the relevant date.
@ref s 4(2) Public company (src:37-39)
GIVEN c IS A `Company profile`
      `requirements as to registration or re-registration as a public company complied with on or after the relevant date` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4(2) the company is a public company` MEANS
    IF       (    c's `liability of the members` EQUALS `liability limited to the amount, if any, unpaid on the shares held`
              OR  c's `liability of the members` EQUALS `liability limited to the amount the members undertake to contribute on a winding up`)
         AND c's `a share capital`
         AND c's `certificate of incorporation stating that it is a public company`
         AND `requirements as to registration or re-registration as a public company complied with on or after the relevant date`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A “public company” is a company limited by shares or limited by guarantee and having a share capital— (a) whose certificate of incorporation states that it is a public company, and (b) in relation to which the requirements of this Act, or the former Companies Acts, as to registration or re-registration as a public company have been complied with on or after the relevant date"

-- src:36 | (1) A “private company” is any company that is not a public company.
@ref s 4(1) Private company (src:36)
GIVEN c IS A `Company profile`
      `requirements as to registration or re-registration as a public company complied with on or after the relevant date` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4(1) the company is a private company` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 4(2) the company is a public company` c `requirements as to registration or re-registration as a public company complied with on or after the relevant date`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A “private company” is any company that is not a public company"
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): follows s 4(2)

-- ---- s 5: Companies limited by guarantee and having share capital ----------------------------------------

-- src:45 | (1) A company cannot be formed as, or become, a company limited by guarantee with a share capital.
@ref s 5(1) Companies limited by guarantee and having share capital (src:45)
GIVEN `the company would be limited by guarantee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company would have a share capital` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 5(1) a company can be formed as, or become, a company limited by guarantee with a share capital` MEANS
    IF `the company would be limited by guarantee` AND `the company would have a share capital`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A company cannot be formed as, or become, a company limited by guarantee with a share capital"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the prohibition names only a company limited by guarantee with a share capital

-- src:46 | (2) Provision to this effect has been in force—
-- src:47 | (a) in Great Britain since 22nd December 1980, and
-- src:48 | (b) in Northern Ireland since 1st July 1983.
@ref s 5(2) Provision in force since (src:46-48)
GIVEN place IS A `Place of registration`
GIVETH A DATE
`s 5(2) the date from which s 5(1) has been in force` MEANS
    CONSIDER place
    WHEN `Northern Ireland` THEN Date 1 7 1983
    OTHERWISE Date 22 12 1980 -- "Great Britain" is England and Wales together with Scotland

-- src:49 | (3) Any provision in the constitution of a company limited by guarantee that purports to divide the company's undertaking into shares or interests is a provision for a share capital.
-- src:50 | This applies whether or not the nominal value or number of the shares or interests is specified by the provision.
@ref s 5(3) A provision for a share capital (src:49-50)
GIVEN `the company is limited by guarantee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provision purports to divide the company's undertaking into shares or interests` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the nominal value or number of the shares or interests is specified by the provision` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 5(3) the constitutional provision is a provision for a share capital` MEANS
    IF `the company is limited by guarantee` AND `the provision purports to divide the company's undertaking into shares or interests`
    THEN JUST TRUE -- the same whether or not `the nominal value or number of the shares or interests is specified by the provision`
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the text names one kind of provision for a share capital and does not say it is the only kind

-- ---- s 6: Community interest companies -------------------------------------------------------------------

DECLARE `s 6(1) way of becoming a community interest company` IS ONE OF
    `s 6(1) being formed as one`
    `s 6(1) becoming one`

-- src:52 | (1) In accordance with Part 2 of the Companies (Audit, Investigations and Community Enterprise) Act 2004 (c. 27)—
-- src:53 | (a) a company limited by shares or a company limited by guarantee and not having a share capital may be formed as or become a community interest company, and
-- src:54 | (b) a company limited by guarantee and having a share capital may become a community interest company.
@ref s 6(1) Community interest companies (src:52-54)
GIVEN liability IS A `Liability of members`
      `a share capital` IS A BOOLEAN
      way IS A `s 6(1) way of becoming a community interest company`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 6(1) the company may be formed as or become a community interest company` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF liability EQUALS `liability limited to the amount, if any, unpaid on the shares held` THEN JUST TRUE -- (a) a company limited by shares, formed or becoming
        IF liability EQUALS `liability limited to the amount the members undertake to contribute on a winding up` AND NOT (`a share capital`) THEN JUST TRUE -- (a) a company limited by guarantee and not having a share capital
        IF liability EQUALS `liability limited to the amount the members undertake to contribute on a winding up` AND `a share capital` AND way EQUALS `s 6(1) becoming one` THEN JUST TRUE -- (b) may become
        IF liability EQUALS `liability limited to the amount the members undertake to contribute on a winding up` AND `a share capital` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (b) says only "may become"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): Part 2 of the Companies (Audit, Investigations and Community Enterprise) Act 2004 is not among the sources

-- src:55 | (2) The other provisions of the Companies Acts have effect subject to that Part.
@ref s 6(2) Other provisions subject to that Part (src:55)
GIVEN `the provision is one of the other provisions of the Companies Acts` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 6(2) the provision has effect subject to Part 2 of the 2004 Act` MEANS
    IF `the provision is one of the other provisions of the Companies Acts`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The other provisions of the Companies Acts"

