-- ---- s 1158: Meaning of "UK-registered company" ---------------------------------------------------------

-- src:16449 | In the Companies Acts“UK-registered company” means a company registered under this Act. The expression does not include an overseas company that has registered particulars under section 1046.
@ref s 1158 Meaning of UK-registered company (src:16449)
GIVEN `registered under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an overseas company that has registered particulars under section 1046` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1158 the company is a UK-registered company` MEANS
    IF `an overseas company that has registered particulars under section 1046`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The expression does not include an overseas company that has registered particulars under section 1046"
    ELSE IF `registered under this Act`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“UK-registered company” means a company registered under this Act"

-- ---- s 1159: Meaning of "subsidiary" etc ----------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 1160 (power to amend by regulations) is machinery: no function (see NOTES.md).
-- s 1159(3): Schedule 6 is in coa29's range (lines 19553-19587); its answers reach this section as INPUTS.

-- One link is the direct relation between a company and the company that may be its holding company.
DECLARE `s 1159(1) link` HAS
    `holding a majority of the voting rights in it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `being a member of it with the right to appoint or remove a majority of its board of directors` IS A BOOLEAN
    `being a member of it and controlling alone, pursuant to an agreement with other members, a majority of the voting rights in it` IS A BOOLEAN

-- A route is the chain of links from the company up to the other company: one link when the other company is the
-- direct holding company, more when it is "a subsidiary of a company that is itself a subsidiary of that other company".
DECLARE `s 1159(1) route` HAS
    `links from the company up to the other company` IS A LIST OF `s 1159(1) link`

-- src:16452 | (1) A company is a “subsidiary” of another company, its “holding company”, if that other company—
-- src:16453 | (a) holds a majority of the voting rights in it, or
-- src:16454 | (b) is a member of it and has the right to appoint or remove a majority of its board of directors, or
-- src:16455 | (c) is a member of it and controls alone, pursuant to an agreement with other members, a majority of the voting rights in it,
@ref s 1159(1)(a)-(c) A direct holding company (src:16452-16455)
GIVEN l IS A `s 1159(1) link`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1159(1)(a)-(c) the other company is directly the holding company of the company` MEANS
    IF       l's `holding a majority of the voting rights in it`
         OR  l's `being a member of it with the right to appoint or remove a majority of its board of directors`
         OR  l's `being a member of it and controlling alone, pursuant to an agreement with other members, a majority of the voting rights in it`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A company is a “subsidiary” of another company, its “holding company”, if that other company— (a) holds a majority of the voting rights in it, or (b) is a member of it and has the right to appoint or remove a majority of its board of directors, or (c) is a member of it and controls alone, pursuant to an agreement with other members, a majority of the voting rights in it"

-- src:16452 | (1) A company is a “subsidiary” of another company, its “holding company”, if that other company—
-- src:16453 | (a) holds a majority of the voting rights in it, or
-- src:16454 | (b) is a member of it and has the right to appoint or remove a majority of its board of directors, or
-- src:16455 | (c) is a member of it and controls alone, pursuant to an agreement with other members, a majority of the voting rights in it,
-- src:16456 | or if it is a subsidiary of a company that is itself a subsidiary of that other company.
@ref s 1159(1) Subsidiary and holding company (src:16452-16456)
GIVEN routes IS A LIST OF `s 1159(1) route`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1159(1) the company is a subsidiary of the other company` MEANS
    IF null routes
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): no relation between the two companies is stated
    ELSE IF any (GIVEN r YIELD `the route holds` r) routes
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if that other company— (a) ... or (b) ... or (c) ... or if it is a subsidiary of a company that is itself a subsidiary of that other company"
    WHERE
        `the route holds` r MEANS
                NOT (null (r's `links from the company up to the other company`))
            AND all (GIVEN l YIELD       l's `holding a majority of the voting rights in it`
                                    OR   l's `being a member of it with the right to appoint or remove a majority of its board of directors`
                                    OR   l's `being a member of it and controlling alone, pursuant to an agreement with other members, a majority of the voting rights in it`)
                    (r's `links from the company up to the other company`)

DECLARE `s 1159(2) member` IS ONE OF
    `s 1159(2) the other company itself`
    `s 1159(2) a wholly-owned subsidiary of the other company`
    `s 1159(2) a person acting on behalf of the other company`
    `s 1159(2) a person acting on behalf of a wholly-owned subsidiary of the other company`
    `s 1159(2) anyone else`

-- src:16457 | (2) A company is a “wholly-owned subsidiary” of another company if it has no members except that other and that other's wholly-owned subsidiaries or persons acting on behalf of that other or its wholly-owned subsidiaries.
@ref s 1159(2) Wholly-owned subsidiary (src:16457)
GIVEN members IS A LIST OF `s 1159(2) member`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1159(2) the company is a wholly-owned subsidiary of the other company` MEANS
    IF any (GIVEN m YIELD m EQUALS `s 1159(2) anyone else`) members
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if it has no members except that other and that other's wholly-owned subsidiaries or persons acting on behalf of that other or its wholly-owned subsidiaries"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:16459 | (4) In this section and that Schedule “company” includes any body corporate.
@ref s 1159(4) "company" includes any body corporate (src:16459)
GIVEN `the body is a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1159(4) the body is a company for the purposes of s 1159 and Schedule 6` MEANS
    IF `the body is a body corporate`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“company” includes any body corporate"

-- ---- s 1161: Meaning of "undertaking" and related expressions --------------------------------------------

-- src:16467 | (1) In the Companies Acts“undertaking” means—
-- src:16468 | (a) a body corporate or partnership, or
-- src:16469 | (b) an unincorporated association carrying on a trade or business, with or without a view to profit.
@ref s 1161(1) Undertaking (src:16467-16469)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of person`
      `the association carries on a trade or business` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1161(1) the entity is an undertaking` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `a company registered under the Companies Act 2006` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `another body corporate incorporated in the United Kingdom` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a body corporate incorporated outside the United Kingdom` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a partnership` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `an unincorporated association` THEN
        IF `the association carries on a trade or business`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“undertaking” means— ... (b) an unincorporated association carrying on a trade or business, with or without a view to profit"
    WHEN `a corporation sole` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“undertaking” means— (a) a body corporate or partnership", read with s 1173(1)(a), which excludes a corporation sole from "body corporate"
    WHEN `an individual` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“undertaking” means—"

-- src:16471 | (a) in relation to an undertaking with capital but no share capital, are to rights to share in the capital of the undertaking; and
@ref s 1161(2)(a) Shares of an undertaking with capital but no share capital (src:16471)
GIVEN `the undertaking has capital but no share capital` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the right is a right to share in the capital of the undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1161(2)(a) the right is a share in the undertaking` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the undertaking has capital but no share capital`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in relation to an undertaking with capital but no share capital"
    ELSE IF `the right is a right to share in the capital of the undertaking`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "references to shares— (a) in relation to an undertaking with capital but no share capital, are to rights to share in the capital of the undertaking"

-- src:16472 | (b) in relation to an undertaking without capital, are to interests—
-- src:16473 | (i) conferring any right to share in the profits or liability to contribute to the losses of the undertaking, or
-- src:16474 | (ii) giving rise to an obligation to contribute to the debts or expenses of the undertaking in the event of a winding up.
@ref s 1161(2)(b) Shares of an undertaking without capital (src:16472-16474)
GIVEN `the undertaking is without capital` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the interest confers a right to share in the profits or a liability to contribute to the losses of the undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the interest gives rise to an obligation to contribute to the debts or expenses of the undertaking in the event of a winding up` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1161(2)(b) the interest is a share in the undertaking` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the undertaking is without capital`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in relation to an undertaking without capital"
    ELSE IF       `the interest confers a right to share in the profits or a liability to contribute to the losses of the undertaking`
              OR  `the interest gives rise to an obligation to contribute to the debts or expenses of the undertaking in the event of a winding up`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "references to shares— ... (b) in relation to an undertaking without capital, are to interests— (i) conferring any right to share in the profits or liability to contribute to the losses of the undertaking, or (ii) giving rise to an obligation to contribute to the debts or expenses of the undertaking in the event of a winding up"

-- src:16475 | (3) Other expressions appropriate to companies shall be construed, in relation to an undertaking which is not a company, as references to the corresponding persons, officers, documents or organs, as the case may be, appropriate to undertakings of that description.
-- src:16476 | This is subject to provision in any specific context providing for the translation of such expressions.
@ref s 1161(3) Expressions appropriate to companies (src:16475-16476)
GIVEN `the undertaking is not a company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a specific context provides for the translation of the expression` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1161(3) the expression appropriate to companies is construed as a reference to the corresponding person, officer, document or organ of the undertaking` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the undertaking is not a company`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in relation to an undertaking which is not a company"
    ELSE IF `a specific context provides for the translation of the expression`
         THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This is subject to provision in any specific context providing for the translation of such expressions"
         ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:16477 | (4) References in the Companies Acts to “fellow subsidiary undertakings” are to undertakings which are subsidiary undertakings of the same parent undertaking but are not parent undertakings or subsidiary undertakings of each other.
@ref s 1161(4) Fellow subsidiary undertakings (src:16477)
GIVEN `both are subsidiary undertakings of the same parent undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN
      `either is a parent undertaking or a subsidiary undertaking of the other` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1161(4) the two undertakings are fellow subsidiary undertakings` MEANS
    IF `both are subsidiary undertakings of the same parent undertaking` AND NOT (`either is a parent undertaking or a subsidiary undertaking of the other`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "References in the Companies Acts to “fellow subsidiary undertakings” are to undertakings which are subsidiary undertakings of the same parent undertaking but are not parent undertakings or subsidiary undertakings of each other"

-- src:16478 | (5) In the Companies Acts “group undertaking”, in relation to an undertaking, means an undertaking which is—
-- src:16479 | (a) a parent undertaking or subsidiary undertaking of that undertaking, or
-- src:16480 | (b) a subsidiary undertaking of any parent undertaking of that undertaking.
@ref s 1161(5) Group undertaking (src:16478-16480)
GIVEN `a parent undertaking or subsidiary undertaking of that undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a subsidiary undertaking of any parent undertaking of that undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1161(5) the undertaking is a group undertaking in relation to the other undertaking` MEANS
    IF `a parent undertaking or subsidiary undertaking of that undertaking` OR `a subsidiary undertaking of any parent undertaking of that undertaking`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“group undertaking”, in relation to an undertaking, means an undertaking which is— (a) a parent undertaking or subsidiary undertaking of that undertaking, or (b) a subsidiary undertaking of any parent undertaking of that undertaking"

-- ---- s 1162: Parent and subsidiary undertakings ----------------------------------------------------------
-- s 1162(1) and (6) are signposts to Schedule 7 (coa29's range, lines 19588-19627); its answers reach this
-- section as INPUTS. A caller combines the answers: a parent undertaking if (2), (4) or (5) answers JUST TRUE.

DECLARE `s 1162 relation` HAS
    `holding a majority of the voting rights in the undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN
    `being a member of the undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the right to appoint or remove a majority of its board of directors` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the right to exercise a dominant influence by virtue of provisions contained in the undertaking's articles` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the right to exercise a dominant influence by virtue of a control contract` IS A BOOLEAN
    `controlling alone, pursuant to an agreement with other shareholders or members, a majority of the voting rights in the undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a subsidiary undertaking of it being a member of that undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN
    `shares in that undertaking being held by a person acting on behalf of it or any of its subsidiary undertakings` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the power to exercise, or actually exercising, dominant influence or control over it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it and the subsidiary undertaking being managed on a unified basis` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a subsidiary undertaking of it being, or to be treated as, a parent undertaking of that undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:16490 | (3) For the purposes of subsection (2) an undertaking shall be treated as a member of another undertaking—
-- src:16491 | (a) if any of its subsidiary undertakings is a member of that undertaking, or
-- src:16492 | (b) if any shares in that other undertaking are held by a person acting on behalf of the undertaking or any of its subsidiary undertakings.
@ref s 1162(3) Treated as a member (src:16490-16492)
GIVEN rel IS A `s 1162 relation`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1162(3) the undertaking is treated as a member of the other undertaking` MEANS
    IF       rel's `being a member of the undertaking`
         OR  rel's `a subsidiary undertaking of it being a member of that undertaking`
         OR  rel's `shares in that undertaking being held by a person acting on behalf of it or any of its subsidiary undertakings`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "an undertaking shall be treated as a member of another undertaking— (a) if any of its subsidiary undertakings is a member of that undertaking, or (b) if any shares in that other undertaking are held by a person acting on behalf of the undertaking or any of its subsidiary undertakings"

-- src:16483 | (2) An undertaking is a parent undertaking in relation to another undertaking, a subsidiary undertaking, if—
-- src:16484 | (a) it holds a majority of the voting rights in the undertaking, or
-- src:16485 | (b) it is a member of the undertaking and has the right to appoint or remove a majority of its board of directors, or
-- src:16486 | (c) it has the right to exercise a dominant influence over the undertaking—
-- src:16487 | (i) by virtue of provisions contained in the undertaking's articles, or
-- src:16488 | (ii) by virtue of a control contract, or
-- src:16489 | (d) it is a member of the undertaking and controls alone, pursuant to an agreement with other shareholders or members, a majority of the voting rights in the undertaking.
@ref s 1162(2) Parent undertaking (src:16483-16489)
GIVEN rel IS A `s 1162 relation`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1162(2) the first undertaking is a parent undertaking of the second` MEANS
    IF       rel's `holding a majority of the voting rights in the undertaking`
         OR  (`treated as a member` AND rel's `the right to appoint or remove a majority of its board of directors`)
         OR  rel's `the right to exercise a dominant influence by virtue of provisions contained in the undertaking's articles`
         OR  rel's `the right to exercise a dominant influence by virtue of a control contract`
         OR  (`treated as a member` AND rel's `controlling alone, pursuant to an agreement with other shareholders or members, a majority of the voting rights in the undertaking`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An undertaking is a parent undertaking in relation to another undertaking, a subsidiary undertaking, if— (a) ... (b) ... (c) ... or (d) ..." (subsection (4) says "also"; see NOTES.md)
    WHERE
        `treated as a member` MEANS
                rel's `being a member of the undertaking`
            OR  rel's `a subsidiary undertaking of it being a member of that undertaking`
            OR  rel's `shares in that undertaking being held by a person acting on behalf of it or any of its subsidiary undertakings`

-- src:16493 | (4) An undertaking is also a parent undertaking in relation to another undertaking, a subsidiary undertaking, if—
-- src:16494 | (a) it has the power to exercise, or actually exercises, dominant influence or control over it, or
-- src:16495 | (b) it and the subsidiary undertaking are managed on a unified basis.
@ref s 1162(4) Parent undertaking: dominant influence or unified management (src:16493-16495)
GIVEN rel IS A `s 1162 relation`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1162(4) the first undertaking is also a parent undertaking of the second` MEANS
    IF       rel's `the power to exercise, or actually exercising, dominant influence or control over it`
         OR  rel's `it and the subsidiary undertaking being managed on a unified basis`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An undertaking is also a parent undertaking in relation to another undertaking, a subsidiary undertaking, if— (a) it has the power to exercise, or actually exercises, dominant influence or control over it, or (b) it and the subsidiary undertaking are managed on a unified basis"

-- src:16496 | (5) A parent undertaking shall be treated as the parent undertaking of undertakings in relation to which any of its subsidiary undertakings are, or are to be treated as, parent undertakings; and references to its subsidiary undertakings shall be construed accordingly.
@ref s 1162(5) Parent undertaking of undertakings of its subsidiary undertakings (src:16496)
GIVEN rel IS A `s 1162 relation`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1162(5) the first undertaking is treated as a parent undertaking of the second` MEANS
    IF rel's `a subsidiary undertaking of it being, or to be treated as, a parent undertaking of that undertaking`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in relation to which any of its subsidiary undertakings are, or are to be treated as, parent undertakings"

-- src:16498 | (7) In this section and that Schedule references to shares, in relation to an undertaking, are to allotted shares.
@ref s 1162(7) References to shares are to allotted shares (src:16498)
GIVEN `the shares are allotted shares` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1162(7) the reference to shares is a reference to the shares` MEANS
    IF `the shares are allotted shares`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "references to shares, in relation to an undertaking, are to allotted shares"

-- ---- s 1163: "Non-cash asset" ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:16501 | (1) In the Companies Acts “non-cash asset” means any property or interest in property, other than cash.
-- src:16502 | For this purpose “cash” includes foreign currency.
@ref s 1163(1) Non-cash asset (src:16501-16502)
GIVEN `the asset is property or an interest in property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the asset is cash` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the asset is foreign currency` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1163(1) the asset is a non-cash asset` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the asset is property or an interest in property`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“non-cash asset” means any property or interest in property, other than cash"
    ELSE IF `the asset is cash` OR `the asset is foreign currency`
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "other than cash. For this purpose “cash” includes foreign currency"
         ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:16503 | (2) A reference to the transfer or acquisition of a non-cash asset includes—
-- src:16504 | (a) the creation or extinction of an estate or interest in, or a right over, any property, and
-- src:16505 | (b) the discharge of a liability of any person, other than a liability for a liquidated sum.
@ref s 1163(2) Transfer or acquisition of a non-cash asset (src:16503-16505)
GIVEN `the act is the creation or extinction of an estate or interest in, or a right over, any property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act is the discharge of a liability of any person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the liability is a liability for a liquidated sum` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1163(2) the act is a transfer or acquisition of a non-cash asset` MEANS
    IF       `the act is the creation or extinction of an estate or interest in, or a right over, any property`
         OR  (`the act is the discharge of a liability of any person` AND NOT (`the liability is a liability for a liquidated sum`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "A reference to the transfer or acquisition of a non-cash asset includes—"; the discharge of a liability for a liquidated sum is outside paragraph (b) and the text does not say it is not a transfer (fork F15 in NOTES.md)

-- ---- s 1164: "banking company" and "banking group" ---------------------------------------------------------
-- s 1164(3) says the definition in (2) must be read with s 22 of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000, any
-- relevant order and Schedule 2 to that Act: those are not among the sources, so the borrowed terms of (2) are INPUTS.

-- src:16508 | (2) “Banking company” means a person who has permission under Part 4A of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 (c. 8) to accept deposits, other than—
-- src:16509 | (a) a person who is not a company, and
-- src:16510 | (b) a person who has such permission only for the purpose of carrying on another regulated activity in accordance with permission under that Part.
@ref s 1164(2) Banking company (src:16508-16510)
GIVEN `the person has permission under Part 4A of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 to accept deposits` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has such permission only for the purpose of carrying on another regulated activity in accordance with permission under that Part` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1164(2) the person is a banking company` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the person has permission under Part 4A of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 to accept deposits`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“Banking company” means a person who has permission under Part 4A of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 (c. 8) to accept deposits"
    ELSE IF NOT (`the person is a company`)
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "other than— (a) a person who is not a company"
         ELSE IF `the person has such permission only for the purpose of carrying on another regulated activity in accordance with permission under that Part`
              THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "other than— ... (b) a person who has such permission only for the purpose of carrying on another regulated activity in accordance with permission under that Part"
              ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:16512 | (4) References to a banking group are to a group where the parent company is a banking company or where—
-- src:16513 | (a) the parent company's principal subsidiary undertakings are wholly or mainly credit institutions, and
-- src:16514 | (b) the parent company does not itself carry on any material business apart from the acquisition, management and disposal of interests in subsidiary undertakings.
-- src:16515 | “Group” here means a parent undertaking and its subsidiary undertakings.
@ref s 1164(4) Banking group (src:16512-16515)
GIVEN `the parent company is a banking company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the parent company's principal subsidiary undertakings are wholly or mainly credit institutions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the parent company itself carries on material business apart from the acquisition, management and disposal of interests in subsidiary undertakings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1164(4) the group is a banking group` MEANS
    IF       `the parent company is a banking company`
         OR  (    `the parent company's principal subsidiary undertakings are wholly or mainly credit institutions`
              AND NOT (`the parent company itself carries on material business apart from the acquisition, management and disposal of interests in subsidiary undertakings`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "References to a banking group are to a group where the parent company is a banking company or where—"

-- src:16517 | (a) a parent company's principal subsidiary undertakings are the subsidiary undertakings of the company whose results or financial position would principally affect the figures shown in the group accounts, and
@ref s 1164(5)(a) Principal subsidiary undertakings (src:16517)
GIVEN `the undertaking is a subsidiary undertaking of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `its results or financial position would principally affect the figures shown in the group accounts` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1164(5)(a) the undertaking is a principal subsidiary undertaking of the parent company` MEANS
    IF `the undertaking is a subsidiary undertaking of the company` AND `its results or financial position would principally affect the figures shown in the group accounts`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a parent company's principal subsidiary undertakings are the subsidiary undertakings of the company whose results or financial position would principally affect the figures shown in the group accounts"

-- src:16518 | (b) the management of interests in subsidiary undertakings includes the provision of services to such undertakings.
@ref s 1164(5)(b) Management of interests includes the provision of services (src:16518)
GIVEN `the activity is the provision of services to such undertakings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1164(5)(b) the activity is management of interests in subsidiary undertakings` MEANS
    IF `the activity is the provision of services to such undertakings`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "the management of interests in subsidiary undertakings includes the provision of services to such undertakings"

-- ---- s 1165: "insurance company" and related expressions --------------------------------------------------
-- s 1165(7) (insurance market activity, s 316(3) of the 2000 Act) and (8) (read with s 22 and Schedule 2 of that Act)
-- are borrowed terms: the facts that depend on them are INPUTS to the functions below.

-- src:16521 | (2) An “authorised insurance company” means a person (whether incorporated or not) who has permission under Part 4A of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 (c. 8) to effect or carry out contracts of insurance.
-- src:16527 | (4) Neither expression includes a friendly society within the meaning of the Friendly Societies Act 1992 (c. 40).
@ref s 1165(2) and (4) Authorised insurance company (src:16521 and src:16527)
GIVEN `the person has permission under Part 4A of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 to effect or carry out contracts of insurance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a friendly society within the meaning of the Friendly Societies Act 1992` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1165(2) the person is an authorised insurance company` MEANS
    IF `the person is a friendly society within the meaning of the Friendly Societies Act 1992`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(4) Neither expression includes a friendly society within the meaning of the Friendly Societies Act 1992"
    ELSE IF `the person has permission under Part 4A of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 to effect or carry out contracts of insurance`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An “authorised insurance company” means a person (whether incorporated or not) who has permission under Part 4A of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 (c. 8) to effect or carry out contracts of insurance"

-- src:16522 | (3) An “insurance company” means—
-- src:16523 | (a) an authorised insurance company, or
-- src:16524 | (b) any other person (whether incorporated or not) who—
-- src:16525 | (i) carries on insurance market activity, or
-- src:16526 | (ii) may effect or carry out contracts of insurance under which the benefits provided by that person are exclusively or primarily benefits in kind in the event of accident to or breakdown of a vehicle.
-- src:16527 | (4) Neither expression includes a friendly society within the meaning of the Friendly Societies Act 1992 (c. 40).
@ref s 1165(3) and (4) Insurance company (src:16522-16526 and src:16527)
GIVEN `the person has permission under Part 4A of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 to effect or carry out contracts of insurance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person carries on insurance market activity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person may effect or carry out contracts of insurance under which the benefits provided are exclusively or primarily benefits in kind in the event of accident to or breakdown of a vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a friendly society within the meaning of the Friendly Societies Act 1992` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1165(3) the person is an insurance company` MEANS
    IF `the person is a friendly society within the meaning of the Friendly Societies Act 1992`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(4) Neither expression includes a friendly society within the meaning of the Friendly Societies Act 1992"
    ELSE IF       `the person has permission under Part 4A of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 to effect or carry out contracts of insurance`
              OR  `the person carries on insurance market activity`
              OR  `the person may effect or carry out contracts of insurance under which the benefits provided are exclusively or primarily benefits in kind in the event of accident to or breakdown of a vehicle`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An “insurance company” means— (a) an authorised insurance company, or (b) any other person (whether incorporated or not) who— (i) carries on insurance market activity, or (ii) may effect or carry out contracts of insurance under which the benefits provided by that person are exclusively or primarily benefits in kind in the event of accident to or breakdown of a vehicle"

-- src:16528 | (5) References to an insurance group are to a group where the parent company is an insurance company or where—
-- src:16529 | (a) the parent company's principal subsidiary undertakings are wholly or mainly insurance companies, and
-- src:16530 | (b) the parent company does not itself carry on any material business apart from the acquisition, management and disposal of interests in subsidiary undertakings.
-- src:16531 | “Group” here means a parent undertaking and its subsidiary undertakings.
@ref s 1165(5) Insurance group (src:16528-16531)
GIVEN `the parent company is an insurance company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the parent company's principal subsidiary undertakings are wholly or mainly insurance companies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the parent company itself carries on material business apart from the acquisition, management and disposal of interests in subsidiary undertakings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1165(5) the group is an insurance group` MEANS
    IF       `the parent company is an insurance company`
         OR  (    `the parent company's principal subsidiary undertakings are wholly or mainly insurance companies`
              AND NOT (`the parent company itself carries on material business apart from the acquisition, management and disposal of interests in subsidiary undertakings`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "References to an insurance group are to a group where the parent company is an insurance company or where—"

-- src:16533 | (a) a parent company's principal subsidiary undertakings are the subsidiary undertakings of the company whose results or financial position would principally affect the figures shown in the group accounts, and
@ref s 1165(6)(a) Principal subsidiary undertakings (src:16533)
GIVEN `the undertaking is a subsidiary undertaking of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `its results or financial position would principally affect the figures shown in the group accounts` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1165(6)(a) the undertaking is a principal subsidiary undertaking of the parent company` MEANS
    IF `the undertaking is a subsidiary undertaking of the company` AND `its results or financial position would principally affect the figures shown in the group accounts`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a parent company's principal subsidiary undertakings are the subsidiary undertakings of the company whose results or financial position would principally affect the figures shown in the group accounts"

-- src:16534 | (b) the management of interests in subsidiary undertakings includes the provision of services to such undertakings.
@ref s 1165(6)(b) Management of interests includes the provision of services (src:16534)
GIVEN `the activity is the provision of services to such undertakings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1165(6)(b) the activity is management of interests in subsidiary undertakings` MEANS
    IF `the activity is the provision of services to such undertakings`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "the management of interests in subsidiary undertakings includes the provision of services to such undertakings"

-- ---- s 1166: "Employees' share scheme" -------------------------------------------------------------------

DECLARE `s 1166 beneficiary` IS ONE OF
    `s 1166 a bona fide employee or former employee of the company`
    `s 1166 a bona fide employee or former employee of a subsidiary of the company`
    `s 1166 a bona fide employee or former employee of the company's holding company or of a subsidiary of the company's holding company`
    `s 1166 a spouse, civil partner, surviving spouse or surviving civil partner of such an employee or former employee`
    `s 1166 a minor child or step-child of such an employee or former employee`
    `s 1166 anyone else`

-- src:16538 | For the purposes of the Companies Acts an employees' share scheme is a scheme for encouraging or facilitating the holding of shares in or debentures of a company by or for the benefit of—
-- src:16539 | (a) the bona fide employees or former employees of—
-- src:16540 | (i) the company,
-- src:16541 | (ii) any subsidiary of the company, or
-- src:16542 | (iii) the company's holding company or any subsidiary of the company's holding company, or
-- src:16543 | (b) the spouses, civil partners, surviving spouses, surviving civil partners, or minor children or step-children of such employees or former employees.
@ref s 1166 Employees' share scheme (src:16538-16543)
GIVEN `the scheme is for encouraging or facilitating the holding of shares in or debentures of a company` IS A BOOLEAN
      beneficiaries IS A LIST OF `s 1166 beneficiary`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1166 the scheme is an employees' share scheme` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the scheme is for encouraging or facilitating the holding of shares in or debentures of a company`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "an employees' share scheme is a scheme for encouraging or facilitating the holding of shares in or debentures of a company"
    ELSE IF any (GIVEN b YIELD b EQUALS `s 1166 anyone else`) beneficiaries
         THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the scheme is "by or for the benefit of" the listed classes and the text does not say whether a scheme that also benefits others is one (fork F17 in NOTES.md)
         ELSE JUST TRUE

-- ---- s 1167: Meaning of "prescribed" ---------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:16545 | In the Companies Acts “prescribed” means prescribed (by order or by regulations) by the Secretary of State.
@ref s 1167 Prescribed (src:16545)
GIVEN `prescribed by order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `prescribed by regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `prescribed by the Secretary of State` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1167 the matter is prescribed` MEANS
    IF (`prescribed by order` OR `prescribed by regulations`) AND `prescribed by the Secretary of State`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“prescribed” means prescribed (by order or by regulations) by the Secretary of State"

-- ---- s 1168: Hard copy and electronic form and related expressions ---------------------------------------
-- s 1168(1) is only the lead-in ("The following provisions apply for the purposes of the Companies Acts").
-- "References to hard copy have a corresponding meaning" (s 1168(2)), "electronic copy" (s 1168(3)) and "electronic
-- means" (s 1168(4)): the same function answers for a reference to the corresponding noun or adjective.

-- src:16548 | (2) A document or information is sent or supplied in hard copy form if it is sent or supplied in a paper copy or similar form capable of being read.
@ref s 1168(2) Hard copy form (src:16548)
GIVEN `sent or supplied in a paper copy or similar form capable of being read` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1168(2) the document or information is sent or supplied in hard copy form` MEANS
    IF `sent or supplied in a paper copy or similar form capable of being read`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A document or information is sent or supplied in hard copy form if it is sent or supplied in a paper copy or similar form capable of being read"

-- src:16550 | (3) A document or information is sent or supplied in electronic form if it is sent or supplied—
-- src:16551 | (a) by electronic means (for example, by e-mail or fax), or
-- src:16552 | (b) by any other means while in an electronic form (for example, sending a disk by post).
@ref s 1168(3) Electronic form (src:16550-16552)
GIVEN `sent or supplied by electronic means` IS A BOOLEAN
      `sent or supplied by any other means while in an electronic form` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1168(3) the document or information is sent or supplied in electronic form` MEANS
    IF `sent or supplied by electronic means` OR `sent or supplied by any other means while in an electronic form`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A document or information is sent or supplied in electronic form if it is sent or supplied— (a) by electronic means (for example, by e-mail or fax), or (b) by any other means while in an electronic form (for example, sending a disk by post)"

-- src:16554 | (4) A document or information is sent or supplied by electronic means if it is—
-- src:16555 | (a) sent initially and received at its destination by means of electronic equipment for the processing (which expression includes digital compression) or storage of data, and
-- src:16556 | (b) entirely transmitted, conveyed and received by wire, by radio, by optical means or by other electromagnetic means.
@ref s 1168(4) Electronic means (src:16554-16556)
GIVEN `sent initially and received at its destination by means of electronic equipment for the processing or storage of data` IS A BOOLEAN
      `entirely transmitted, conveyed and received by wire, by radio, by optical means or by other electromagnetic means` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1168(4) the document or information is sent or supplied by electronic means` MEANS
    IF `sent initially and received at its destination by means of electronic equipment for the processing or storage of data` AND `entirely transmitted, conveyed and received by wire, by radio, by optical means or by other electromagnetic means`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A document or information is sent or supplied by electronic means if it is— (a) sent initially and received at its destination by means of electronic equipment for the processing (which expression includes digital compression) or storage of data, and (b) entirely transmitted, conveyed and received by wire, by radio, by optical means or by other electromagnetic means"

-- src:16558 | (5) A document or information authorised or required to be sent or supplied in electronic form must be sent or supplied in a form, and by a means, that the sender or supplier reasonably considers will enable the recipient—
-- src:16559 | (a) to read it, and
-- src:16560 | (b) to retain a copy of it.
@ref s 1168(5) The sender must use a form and means the recipient can read and retain (src:16558-16560)
GIVEN `the document or information is authorised or required to be sent or supplied in electronic form` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the sender or supplier reasonably considers the form and means will enable the recipient to read it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the sender or supplier reasonably considers the form and means will enable the recipient to retain a copy of it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1168(5) the sender or supplier has used a form and means the section allows` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the document or information is authorised or required to be sent or supplied in electronic form`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "authorised or required to be sent or supplied in electronic form"
    ELSE IF `the sender or supplier reasonably considers the form and means will enable the recipient to read it` AND `the sender or supplier reasonably considers the form and means will enable the recipient to retain a copy of it`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be sent or supplied in a form, and by a means, that the sender or supplier reasonably considers will enable the recipient— (a) to read it, and (b) to retain a copy of it"

-- src:16561 | (6) For the purposes of this section, a document or information can be read only if—
-- src:16562 | (a) it can be read with the naked eye, or
-- src:16563 | (b) to the extent that it consists of images (for example photographs, pictures, maps, plans or drawings), it can be seen with the naked eye.
@ref s 1168(6) Can be read (src:16561-16563)
GIVEN `it can be read with the naked eye` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it consists of images` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the images can be seen with the naked eye` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1168(6) the document or information can be read` MEANS
    IF       `it can be read with the naked eye`
         OR  (`it consists of images` AND `the images can be seen with the naked eye`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a document or information can be read only if— (a) it can be read with the naked eye, or (b) to the extent that it consists of images ... it can be seen with the naked eye"

DECLARE `s 1168(7) word used by the provision` IS ONE OF
    `s 1168(7) sent`
    `s 1168(7) supplied`
    `s 1168(7) deliver`
    `s 1168(7) provide`
    `s 1168(7) produce`
    `s 1168(7) give, of a notice`
    `s 1168(7) another word`

-- src:16564 | (7) The provisions of this section apply whether the provision of the Companies Acts in question uses the words “sent” or “supplied” or uses other words (such as “deliver”, “provide”, “produce” or, in the case of a notice, “give”) to refer to the sending or supplying of a document or information.
@ref s 1168(7) The section applies whatever word is used (src:16564)
GIVEN word IS A `s 1168(7) word used by the provision`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1168(7) the provisions of s 1168 apply to the provision of the Companies Acts` MEANS
    CONSIDER word
    WHEN `s 1168(7) sent` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 1168(7) supplied` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 1168(7) deliver` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 1168(7) provide` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 1168(7) produce` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 1168(7) give, of a notice` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 1168(7) another word` THEN JUST TRUE -- "whether the provision ... uses the words “sent” or “supplied” or uses other words (such as ...)": the examples do not limit the words

-- ---- s 1169: Dormant companies ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 1169(2) needs s 386 (accounting records, coa8's range): its answer arrives as an INPUT.

-- src:16566 | (1) For the purposes of the Companies Acts a company is “dormant” during any period in which it has no significant accounting transaction.
@ref s 1169(1) Dormant company (src:16566)
GIVEN `the company has no significant accounting transaction in the period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1169(1) the company is dormant during the period` MEANS
    IF `the company has no significant accounting transaction in the period`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a company is “dormant” during any period in which it has no significant accounting transaction"

-- src:16567 | (2) A “significant accounting transaction” means a transaction that is required by section 386 to be entered in the company's accounting records.
@ref s 1169(2) Significant accounting transaction (src:16567)
GIVEN `the transaction is required by section 386 to be entered in the company's accounting records` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1169(2) the transaction is a significant accounting transaction` MEANS
    IF `the transaction is required by section 386 to be entered in the company's accounting records`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A “significant accounting transaction” means a transaction that is required by section 386 to be entered in the company's accounting records"

DECLARE `s 1169(3) kind of transaction` IS ONE OF
    `s 1169(3) the taking of shares by a subscriber to the memorandum as a result of an undertaking in connection with the formation of the company`
    `s 1169(3) the payment of a fee to the registrar on a change of the company's name`
    `s 1169(3) the payment of a fee to the registrar on the re-registration of the company`
    `s 1169(3) the payment of a penalty under section 453`
    `s 1169(3) the payment of a fee to the registrar for the registration of a confirmation statement`
    `s 1169(3) any other transaction`

-- src:16568 | (3) In determining whether or when a company is dormant, there shall be disregarded—
-- src:16569 | (a) any transaction arising from the taking of shares in the company by a subscriber to the memorandum as a result of an undertaking of his in connection with the formation of the company;
-- src:16570 | (b) any transaction consisting of the payment of—
-- src:16571 | (i) a fee to the registrar on a change of the company's name,
-- src:16572 | (ii) a fee to the registrar on the re-registration of the company,
-- src:16573 | (iii) a penalty under section 453 (penalty for failure to file accounts), or
-- src:16574 | (iv) a fee to the registrar for the registration of a confirmation statement.
@ref s 1169(3) Transactions disregarded (src:16568-16574)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 1169(3) kind of transaction`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1169(3) the transaction is disregarded in determining whether or when the company is dormant` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `s 1169(3) any other transaction` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the list of disregarded transactions is not closed with "only"
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:16575 | (4) Any reference in the Companies Acts to a body corporate other than a company being dormant has a corresponding meaning.
@ref s 1169(4) A body corporate other than a company is dormant (src:16575)
GIVEN `the body is a body corporate other than a company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body has no transaction corresponding to a significant accounting transaction in the period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1169(4) the body corporate other than a company is dormant during the period` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the body is a body corporate other than a company`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a body corporate other than a company"
    ELSE IF `the body has no transaction corresponding to a significant accounting transaction in the period`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "has a corresponding meaning" (read with s 1169(1): "“dormant” during any period in which it has no significant accounting transaction")

-- ---- s 1170: "EEA State" and related expressions -------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:16578 | “ EEA State ” has the meaning given by Schedule 1 to the Interpretation Act 1978;
@ref s 1170 EEA State (src:16578)
GIVEN `within the meaning given by Schedule 1 to the Interpretation Act 1978` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1170 the State is an EEA State` MEANS
    CONSIDER `within the meaning given by Schedule 1 to the Interpretation Act 1978`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the borrowed definition says no, supplied as an input): "has the meaning given by Schedule 1 to the Interpretation Act 1978"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the Interpretation Act 1978 is not among the sources

-- src:16579 | “ EEA company” and “ EEA undertaking” mean a company or undertaking governed by the law of an EEA State.
@ref s 1170 EEA company and EEA undertaking (src:16579)
GIVEN `the company or undertaking is governed by the law of an EEA State` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1170 the company or undertaking is an EEA company or EEA undertaking` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the company or undertaking is governed by the law of an EEA State`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "mean a company or undertaking governed by the law of an EEA State"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): "EEA State" is defined by the Interpretation Act 1978, outside the sources

-- ---- s 1170A: Receiver or manager and certain related references ------------------------------------------

DECLARE `s 1170A(1) what the person is a receiver or manager of` IS ONE OF
    `s 1170A(1) the property of the company`
    `s 1170A(1) part only of the property of the company`
    `s 1170A(1) only the income arising from the property`
    `s 1170A(1) only the income arising from part of the property`
    `s 1170A(1) something else`

-- src:16581 | (1) Any reference in the Companies Acts to a receiver or manager of the property of a company, or to a receiver of it, includes a receiver or manager or (as the case may be) a receiver of part only of that property and a receiver only of the income arising from the property or from part of it.
@ref s 1170A(1) Receiver or manager of part of the property (src:16581)
GIVEN subject IS A `s 1170A(1) what the person is a receiver or manager of`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1170A(1) the reference to a receiver or manager of the property of a company, or to a receiver of it, covers the person` MEANS
    CONSIDER subject
    WHEN `s 1170A(1) something else` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "includes a receiver or manager or (as the case may be) a receiver of part only of that property and a receiver only of the income arising from the property or from part of it"
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:16582 | (2) Any reference in the Companies Acts to the appointment of a receiver or manager under powers contained in an instrument includes an appointment made under powers that by virtue of an enactment are implied in and have effect as if contained in an instrument.
@ref s 1170A(2) Appointment under implied powers (src:16582)
GIVEN `the appointment is made under powers contained in an instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appointment is made under powers that by virtue of an enactment are implied in and have effect as if contained in an instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1170A(2) the reference to the appointment of a receiver or manager under powers contained in an instrument covers the appointment` MEANS
    IF       `the appointment is made under powers contained in an instrument`
         OR  `the appointment is made under powers that by virtue of an enactment are implied in and have effect as if contained in an instrument`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "includes an appointment made under powers that by virtue of an enactment are implied in and have effect as if contained in an instrument"

-- ---- s 1170B: Meaning of "contributory" -------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:16584 | (1) In the Companies Acts “ contributory ” means every person liable to contribute to the assets of a company in the event of its being wound up.
-- src:16585 | (2) For the purposes of all proceedings for determining, and all proceedings prior to the final determination of, the persons who are to be deemed contributories, the expression includes any person alleged to be a contributory.
-- src:16586 | (3) The reference in subsection (1) to persons liable to contribute to the assets does not include a person so liable by virtue of a declaration by the court under—
-- src:16587 | (a) section 213 of the Insolvency Act 1986 or Article 177 of the Insolvency (Northern Ireland) Order 1989 (fraudulent trading), or
-- src:16588 | (b) section 214 of that Act or Article 178 of that Order (wrongful trading).
@ref s 1170B Contributory (src:16584-16588)
GIVEN `the person is liable to contribute to the assets of the company in the event of its being wound up` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is liable only by virtue of a declaration of the court under section 213 of the Insolvency Act 1986 or Article 177 of the Insolvency (Northern Ireland) Order 1989 (fraudulent trading)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is liable only by virtue of a declaration of the court under section 214 of that Act or Article 178 of that Order (wrongful trading)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceedings are proceedings for determining, or prior to the final determination of, the persons to be deemed contributories` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is alleged to be a contributory` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1170B the person is a contributory` MEANS
    IF `the proceedings are proceedings for determining, or prior to the final determination of, the persons to be deemed contributories` AND `the person is alleged to be a contributory`
    THEN JUST TRUE -- (2) "the expression includes any person alleged to be a contributory" (fork F21 in NOTES.md: subsection (3) is read as qualifying only subsection (1))
    ELSE IF `the person is liable only by virtue of a declaration of the court under section 213 of the Insolvency Act 1986 or Article 177 of the Insolvency (Northern Ireland) Order 1989 (fraudulent trading)` OR `the person is liable only by virtue of a declaration of the court under section 214 of that Act or Article 178 of that Order (wrongful trading)`
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The reference in subsection (1) to persons liable to contribute to the assets does not include a person so liable by virtue of a declaration by the court under— (a) section 213 ... (fraudulent trading), or (b) section 214 ... (wrongful trading)"
         ELSE IF `the person is liable to contribute to the assets of the company in the event of its being wound up`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means every person liable to contribute to the assets of a company in the event of its being wound up"

-- ---- s 1171: The former Companies Acts -------------------------------------------------------------------

DECLARE `s 1171 enactment` IS ONE OF
    `s 1171 a Joint Stock Companies Act`
    `s 1171 the Companies Act 1862`
    `s 1171 the Companies (Consolidation) Act 1908`
    `s 1171 the Companies Act 1929`
    `s 1171 the Companies Act (Northern Ireland) 1932`
    `s 1171 the Companies Acts 1948 to 1983`
    `s 1171 the Companies Act (Northern Ireland) 1960`
    `s 1171 the Companies (Northern Ireland) Order 1986`
    `s 1171 the Companies Consolidation (Consequential Provisions) (Northern Ireland) Order 1986`
    `s 1171 a provision of the Companies Act 1985`
    `s 1171 a provision of the Companies Consolidation (Consequential Provisions) Act 1985`
    `s 1171 another enactment`

-- src:16591 | “the former Companies Acts” means—
-- src:16592 | (a) the Joint Stock Companies Acts, the Companies Act 1862 (c. 89), the Companies (Consolidation) Act 1908 (c. 69), the Companies Act 1929 (c. 23), the Companies Act (Northern Ireland) 1932 (c. 7 (N.I.)), the Companies Acts 1948 to 1983, the Companies Act (Northern Ireland) 1960 (c. 22 (N.I.)), the Companies (Northern Ireland) Order 1986 (S.I. 1986/1032 (N.I. 6)) and the Companies Consolidation (Consequential Provisions) (Northern Ireland) Order 1986 (S.I. 1986/1035 (N.I. 9)), and
-- src:16593 | (b) the provisions of the Companies Act 1985 (c. 6) and the Companies Consolidation (Consequential Provisions) Act 1985 (c. 9) that are no longer in force;
@ref s 1171 The former Companies Acts (src:16591-16593)
GIVEN enactment IS A `s 1171 enactment`
      `the provision is no longer in force` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1171 the enactment is one of the former Companies Acts` MEANS
    CONSIDER enactment
    WHEN `s 1171 a provision of the Companies Act 1985` THEN
        IF `the provision is no longer in force`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) the provisions of the Companies Act 1985 (c. 6) and the Companies Consolidation (Consequential Provisions) Act 1985 (c. 9) that are no longer in force"
    WHEN `s 1171 a provision of the Companies Consolidation (Consequential Provisions) Act 1985` THEN
        IF `the provision is no longer in force`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) the provisions of the Companies Act 1985 (c. 6) and the Companies Consolidation (Consequential Provisions) Act 1985 (c. 9) that are no longer in force"
    WHEN `s 1171 another enactment` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“the former Companies Acts” means—"
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE -- the Acts and Orders named in paragraph (a)

DECLARE `s 1171 Act` IS ONE OF
    `s 1171 the Joint Stock Companies Act 1856`
    `s 1171 the Joint Stock Companies Acts 1856, 1857`
    `s 1171 the Joint Stock Banking Companies Act 1857`
    `s 1171 the Act to enable Joint Stock Banking Companies to be formed on the principle of limited liability (1858 c. 91)`
    `s 1171 the Joint Stock Companies Act 1844`
    `s 1171 another Act`

-- src:16594 | “the Joint Stock Companies Acts” means the Joint Stock Companies Act 1856 (c. 47), the Joint Stock Companies Acts 1856, 1857 (20 & 21 Vict. c. 14), the Joint Stock Banking Companies Act 1857 (c. 49), and the Act to enable Joint Stock Banking Companies to be formed on the principle of limited liability (1858 c. 91), but does not include the Joint Stock Companies Act 1844 (c. 110).
@ref s 1171 The Joint Stock Companies Acts (src:16594)
GIVEN act IS A `s 1171 Act`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1171 the Act is one of the Joint Stock Companies Acts` MEANS
    CONSIDER act
    WHEN `s 1171 the Joint Stock Companies Act 1844` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "but does not include the Joint Stock Companies Act 1844 (c. 110)"
    WHEN `s 1171 another Act` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“the Joint Stock Companies Acts” means the Joint Stock Companies Act 1856 (c. 47), the Joint Stock Companies Acts 1856, 1857 (20 & 21 Vict. c. 14), the Joint Stock Banking Companies Act 1857 (c. 49), and the Act to enable Joint Stock Banking Companies to be formed on the principle of limited liability (1858 c. 91)"
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- ---- s 1172: References to requirements of this Act ------------------------------------------------------

-- src:16597 | References in the company law provisions of this Act to the requirements of this Act include the requirements of regulations and orders made under it.
@ref s 1172 References to requirements of this Act (src:16597)
GIVEN `the reference is in the company law provisions of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirement is a requirement of regulations made under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirement is a requirement of an order made under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1172 the reference to the requirements of this Act covers the requirement` MEANS
    IF `the reference is in the company law provisions of this Act` AND (`the requirement is a requirement of regulations made under this Act` OR `the requirement is a requirement of an order made under this Act`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "include the requirements of regulations and orders made under it"; a reference outside the company law provisions is not mentioned

-- ---- s 1173: Minor definitions: general (subsection (1) only; subsection (2) is blank in this text) ---------

-- src:16600 | “the Audit Regulation” means Regulation 537/2014 of the European Parliament and of the Council on specific requirements regarding statutory audit of public interest entities;
@ref s 1173(1) The Audit Regulation (src:16600)
GIVEN `the instrument is Regulation 537/2014 of the European Parliament and of the Council on specific requirements regarding statutory audit of public interest entities` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1173(1) the instrument is the Audit Regulation` MEANS
    IF `the instrument is Regulation 537/2014 of the European Parliament and of the Council on specific requirements regarding statutory audit of public interest entities`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“the Audit Regulation” means Regulation 537/2014 of the European Parliament and of the Council on specific requirements regarding statutory audit of public interest entities"

-- src:16601 | “body corporate” and “corporation” include a body incorporated outside the United Kingdom, but do not include—
-- src:16602 | (a) a corporation sole, or
-- src:16603 | (b) a partnership that, whether or not a legal person, is not regarded as a body corporate under the law by which it is governed;
@ref s 1173(1) Body corporate and corporation (src:16601-16603)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of person`
      `a partnership regarded as a body corporate under the law by which it is governed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1173(1) the person is a body corporate or a corporation` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `a body corporate incorporated outside the United Kingdom` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a corporation sole` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "but do not include— (a) a corporation sole"
    WHEN `a partnership` THEN
        IF `a partnership regarded as a body corporate under the law by which it is governed`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): the exclusion in paragraph (b) does not reach a partnership regarded as a body corporate, and the text does not say it is one
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "but do not include— ... (b) a partnership that, whether or not a legal person, is not regarded as a body corporate under the law by which it is governed"
    WHEN `a company registered under the Companies Act 2006` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): the definition says only what it includes and excludes beyond the ordinary meaning
    WHEN `another body corporate incorporated in the United Kingdom` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): as for a company registered under this Act
    WHEN `an individual` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent)
    WHEN `an unincorporated association` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent)

-- src:16604 | “the competent authority” means the Financial Reporting Council Limited;
@ref s 1173(1) The competent authority (src:16604)
GIVEN `the body is the Financial Reporting Council Limited` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1173(1) the body is the competent authority` MEANS
    IF `the body is the Financial Reporting Council Limited`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“the competent authority” means the Financial Reporting Council Limited"

-- The terms the text hands to another instrument: credit institution (Regulation (EU) No. 575/2013, Article 4(1)(1));
-- the data protection legislation (Data Protection Act 2018, s 3); EU regulated market (Regulation (EU) No. 600/2014,
-- Article 2.1.13B); financial institution (Bank Branches Directive 89/117/EEC, Article 1.1); hire-purchase agreement
-- (Consumer Credit Act 1974); regulated activity (Financial Services and Markets Act 2000, s 22); regulated market
-- (Article 2.1.13); transferable securities (Article 2.1.24); UK regulated market (Article 2.1.13A).
DECLARE `s 1173(1) borrowed term` IS ONE OF
    `s 1173(1) credit institution`
    `s 1173(1) the data protection legislation`
    `s 1173(1) EU regulated market`
    `s 1173(1) financial institution`
    `s 1173(1) hire-purchase agreement`
    `s 1173(1) regulated activity`
    `s 1173(1) regulated market`
    `s 1173(1) transferable securities`
    `s 1173(1) UK regulated market`

-- src:16605 | “credit institution” means a credit institution as defined in Article 4(1)(1) of Regulation ( EU ) No. 575/2013 of the European Parliament and of the Council.
-- src:16606 | “the data protection legislation” has the same meaning as in the Data Protection Act 2018 (see section 3 of that Act);
-- src:16607 | “EU regulated market” has the meaning given in Article 2.1.13B of Regulation (EU) No. 600/2014 of the European Parliament and of the Council of 15 May 2014 and amending Regulation (EU) No. 648/2012;
-- src:16608 | “financial institution” means a financial institution within the meaning of Article 1.1 of the Council Directive on the obligations of branches established in a Member State of credit and financial institutions having their head offices outside that Member State regarding the publication of annual accounting documents (the Bank Branches Directive, 89/117/EEC);
-- src:16614 | “hire-purchase agreement” has the same meaning as in the Consumer Credit Act 1974 (c. 39);
-- src:16617 | “regulated activity” has the meaning given in section 22 of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 (c. 8);
-- src:16618 | “regulated market” has the meaning given in Article 2.1.13 of Regulation (EU) No. 600/2014 of the European Parliament and of the Council of 15 May 2014 and amending Regulation (EU) No. 648/2012; ;
-- src:16619 | “transferable securities” has the meaning given by Article 2.1.24 of Regulation (EU) No. 600/2014 of the European Parliament and of the Council of 15 May 2014 and amending Regulation (EU) No. 648/2012;
-- src:16620 | “UK regulated market” has the meaning given in Article 2.1.13A of Regulation (EU) No. 600/2014 of the European Parliament and of the Council of 15 May 2014 and amending Regulation (EU) No. 648/2012;
@ref s 1173(1) Terms defined by another instrument (src:16605-16608 and src:16614 and src:16617-16620)
GIVEN term IS A `s 1173(1) borrowed term`
      `the borrowed instrument says the thing is within the term` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1173(1) the thing is within the borrowed term` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the borrowed instrument says the thing is within the term`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the borrowed definition says no, supplied as an input): the text hands the term to the instrument named for it above
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the instrument that defines the term is not among the sources

-- src:16609 | “firm” means any entity, whether or not a legal person, that is not an individual and includes a body corporate, a corporation sole and a partnership or other unincorporated association;
@ref s 1173(1) Firm (src:16609)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of person`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1173(1) the entity is a firm` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `an individual` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“firm” means any entity, whether or not a legal person, that is not an individual"
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

DECLARE `s 1173(1) Gazette` IS ONE OF
    `s 1173(1) the London Gazette`
    `s 1173(1) the Edinburgh Gazette`
    `s 1173(1) the Belfast Gazette`

-- The one total table in this module: the text names a Gazette for each of the three places and no other.
-- src:16610 | “the Gazette” means—
-- src:16611 | (a) as respects companies registered in England and Wales, the London Gazette,
-- src:16612 | (b) as respects companies registered in Scotland, the Edinburgh Gazette, and
-- src:16613 | (c) as respects companies registered in Northern Ireland, the Belfast Gazette;
@ref s 1173(1) The Gazette (src:16610-16613)
GIVEN place IS A `Place of registration`
GIVETH A `s 1173(1) Gazette`
`s 1173(1) the Gazette for a company registered in the place` MEANS
    CONSIDER place
    WHEN `England and Wales` THEN `s 1173(1) the London Gazette`
    WHEN `Scotland` THEN `s 1173(1) the Edinburgh Gazette`
    WHEN `Northern Ireland` THEN `s 1173(1) the Belfast Gazette`

DECLARE `s 1173(1) position in the body corporate` IS ONE OF
    `s 1173(1) director`
    `s 1173(1) manager`
    `s 1173(1) secretary`
    `s 1173(1) another position`

-- src:16615 | “officer”, in relation to a body corporate, includes a director, manager or secretary;
@ref s 1173(1) Officer (src:16615)
GIVEN position IS A `s 1173(1) position in the body corporate`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1173(1) the holder of the position is an officer of the body corporate` MEANS
    CONSIDER position
    WHEN `s 1173(1) another position` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“officer”, in relation to a body corporate, includes a director, manager or secretary"
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:16616 | “parent company” means a company that is a parent undertaking (see section 1162 and Schedule 7);
@ref s 1173(1) Parent company (src:16616)
GIVEN `the person is a company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is a parent undertaking (section 1162 and Schedule 7)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1173(1) the company is a parent company` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the person is a company`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“parent company” means a company that is a parent undertaking"
    ELSE CONSIDER `the company is a parent undertaking (section 1162 and Schedule 7)`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“parent company” means a company that is a parent undertaking"
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the company is a parent undertaking is s 1162 together with Schedule 7, which a caller answers

-- src:16621 | “working day”, in relation to a company, means a day that is not a Saturday or Sunday, Christmas Day, Good Friday or any day that is a bank holiday under the Banking and Financial Dealings Act 1971 (c. 80) in the part of the United Kingdom where the company is registered.
@ref s 1173(1) Working day (src:16621)
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
      `the place where the company is registered` IS A `Place of registration`
      `the day is Good Friday` IS A BOOLEAN
      `bank holidays under the Banking and Financial Dealings Act 1971 in England and Wales` IS A LIST OF DATE
      `bank holidays under the Banking and Financial Dealings Act 1971 in Scotland` IS A LIST OF DATE
      `bank holidays under the Banking and Financial Dealings Act 1971 in Northern Ireland` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1173(1) the day is a working day for the company` MEANS
    IF       `is weekend` `the day`
         OR  (DATE_MONTH `the day` EQUALS 12 AND DATE_DAY `the day` EQUALS 25)
         OR  `the day is Good Friday`
         OR  elem `the day` `bank holidays in the place`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“working day”, in relation to a company, means a day that is not a Saturday or Sunday, Christmas Day, Good Friday or any day that is a bank holiday under the Banking and Financial Dealings Act 1971 (c. 80) in the part of the United Kingdom where the company is registered"
    ELSE JUST TRUE
    WHERE
        `bank holidays in the place` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the place where the company is registered`
            WHEN `England and Wales` THEN `bank holidays under the Banking and Financial Dealings Act 1971 in England and Wales`
            WHEN `Scotland` THEN `bank holidays under the Banking and Financial Dealings Act 1971 in Scotland`
            WHEN `Northern Ireland` THEN `bank holidays under the Banking and Financial Dealings Act 1971 in Northern Ireland`
